1
00:00:01,038 --> 00:00:02,080
x86。
X86.

2
00:00:02,510 --> 00:00:07,940
x86 是几乎所有 Windows 电脑和笔记本电脑内部的 CPU 架构。
X86 is the CPU architecture inside almost every Windows PC and laptop.

3
00:00:08,206 --> 00:00:10,628
但首先，架构到底是什么意思？
But first, what does architecture even mean?

4
00:00:10,958 --> 00:00:14,820
基本上，CPU 架构就是处理器所使用的语言。
Basically, a CPU architecture is the language a processor speaks.

5
00:00:15,374 --> 00:00:22,916
它是芯片能理解的基础指令列表，比如“把这两个数字相加”、
“把这些数据移到那里”或者“比较这两个数值”。
It's the list of basic commands the chip understands, like add these
two numbers, move this data over there, or compare these two values.

6
00:00:23,374 --> 00:00:26,500
你使用的每个应用最终都会被转换成这些指令。
Every app you use eventually gets turned into these commands.

7
00:00:27,086 --> 00:00:36,000
这就是为什么为一种架构编写的程序不能直接在另一种架构上运行，
就像用日语写的书对于只会说西班牙语的人来说毫无意义一样。
That's why a program made for one architecture can't just run on another one, the same
way a book written in Japanese won't make sense to someone who only reads Spanish.

8
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:50,244
x86 起源于 1978 年的 Intel 8086，这个名字源于那颗芯片以及随后的 8286、
8386 和 8486 等芯片，它们都以 86 结尾。
X86 started in 1978 with the Intel 8086, and the name comes from that chip and
the ones that followed it, like the 8286, 8386, and 8486, which all ended in 86.

9
00:00:50,702 --> 00:00:57,920
然后在 1981 年，IBM 为其第一台个人电脑选择了那颗芯片的近亲——8088。
Then in 1981, IBM picked a close sibling of that chip, the 8088, for its very first personal computer.

10
00:00:58,190 --> 00:01:06,404
那台 IBM PC 被大量的其他制造商仿制，而每一个
仿制品都需要一颗 x86 芯片才能运行相同的软件。
That IBM PC got copied by tons of other manufacturers, and every one of those copies needed an X86 chip to run the same software.

11
00:01:06,798 --> 00:01:09,668
这就是 x86 统治 PC 世界的方式。
And that's how X86 took over the PC world.

12
00:01:09,934 --> 00:01:13,440
让 x86 脱颖而出的特点是向后兼容性。
What makes X86 stand out is backward compatibility.

13
00:01:13,646 --> 00:01:24,164
每一代新产品仍然说旧语言，所以现代的 Intel 或 AMD
处理器仍然能理解为 1978 年最初的 8086 编写的指令。
Every new generation still speaks the old language, so a modern Intel or AMD
processor can still understand instructions written for the original 8086 from 1978.

14
00:01:24,590 --> 00:01:29,760
有趣的是，x86 最重大的升级甚至不是来自 Intel。
And the funny thing is, the biggest upgrade to x86 didn't even come from Intel.

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:38,960
2003 年，AMD 将 x86 扩展到了 64 位，这基本上
就是让你的电脑能够使用远超 4GB 的内存的原因。
In 2003, AMD extended x86 to 64-bit, which is basically what allows your computer to use way more than 4GB of RAM.

16
00:01:39,406 --> 00:01:44,560
Intel 最终采用了 AMD 的版本，而这几乎就是今天所有 PC 所使用的版本。
Intel ended up adopting AMD's version, and that's what pretty much every PC uses today.

17
00:01:44,846 --> 00:01:47,972
Intel 和 AMD 都在生产 x86 芯片。
Both Intel and AMD make x86 chips.

18
00:01:48,334 --> 00:01:54,884
它们在内部设计上有所不同，但它们说同样的语言，就像两个口音不同的人一样。
They design their processors differently on the inside, but they speak the same language,
kind of like two people with different accents.

19
00:01:55,214 --> 00:01:59,716
这就是为什么 Windows 能在两者上运行，而且 x86 不仅仅存在于 PC 中。
That's why Windows runs on both, and x86 isn't just in PCs.

20
00:02:00,334 --> 00:02:07,204
PlayStation 5、Xbox Series X 以及运行互联网的大量服务器也都在使用 x86。
The PlayStation 5, the Xbox Series X, and a huge number of the servers that run the internet use x86 too.

21
00:02:07,534 --> 00:02:10,080
然而，所有的兼容性都伴随着负担。
However, all that compatibility comes with baggage.

22
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:16,132
x86 被称为 CISC 架构，即“复杂指令集计算机”。
X86 is what's called a Cisq architecture, which stands for Complex Instruction Set Computer.

23
00:02:16,334 --> 00:02:21,700
在近 50 年里，它一直在不断增加更多的指令，同时保留所有旧的指令。
For almost 50 years, it kept adding more and more instructions while keeping all the old ones around.

24
00:02:22,158 --> 00:02:33,476
这增加了芯片的额外复杂性，这也是为什么 x86 笔记本在历史上很难达到基于更简单架构的芯片
那样的电池续航时间，我们稍后会讲到这一点。
This adds extra complexity to the chip, and it's one of the reasons x86 laptops have historically had a harder time matching the
battery life of chips built on simpler architectures, which we'll get to later.

25
00:02:34,606 --> 00:02:39,940
6502。6502 是让家用电脑变得负担得起的芯片。
6502 The 6502 is the chip that made home computers affordable.

26
00:02:40,206 --> 00:02:46,852
它由一家名为 Moss Technology 的小公司于 1975 年发布，而它最疯狂的一点就是价格。
It was released in 1975 by a small company called Moss Technology, and the crazy thing about it was the price.

27
00:02:47,502 --> 00:02:56,880
那时，来自 Intel 和 Motorola 的竞争芯片售价在
175 到 180 美元左右，但 6502 的售价仅为 25 美元。
Back then, competing chips from Intel and Motorola cost around $175 to $180, but the 6502 sold for just $25.

28
00:02:57,678 --> 00:03:06,756
在 1975 年的发布展会上，他们甚至不被允许在展厅内销售芯片，
所以他们是从酒店套房里从大玻璃罐里直接卖出的。
At its launch trade show in 1975, they weren't even allowed to sell chips on the show floor,
so they sold them out of a hotel suite straight from big glass jars.

29
00:03:07,086 --> 00:03:10,480
价格低到许多人都不相信这是真的。
The price was so low that a lot of people didn't believe it was real.

30
00:03:10,670 --> 00:03:14,240
正因为它如此便宜，6502 最终出现在了到处。
Because it was so cheap, the 6502 ended up everywhere.

31
00:03:14,734 --> 00:03:17,828
Steve Wozniak 在 Apple I 和 Apple II 中使用了它。
Steve Wozniak used it in the Apple I and Apple II.

32
00:03:18,190 --> 00:03:24,400
Commodore 在 Commodore 64 中使用了一个版本，这款机器常被认为是史上最畅销的家用电脑。
Commodore used a version of it in the Commodore 64, which is often called the best-selling home computer of all time.

33
00:03:24,750 --> 00:03:31,844
Atari 在 Atari 2600 中使用了一个精简版，而任天堂的 NES 也是基于它构建的定制芯片运行的。
Atari used a cut-down version in the Atari 2600, and Nintendo's NES ran on a custom chip built around it too.

34
00:03:32,238 --> 00:03:39,236
6502 是一款 8 位处理器，这意味着它一次只能处理到 255 的数字。
The 6502 is an 8-bit processor, which means it can only handle numbers up to 255 in one step.

35
00:03:39,470 --> 00:03:41,220
按今天的标准来看，这非常微小。
That's tiny by today's standards.

36
00:03:41,518 --> 00:03:46,084
为了压低价格，设计师去掉了所有非核心的必要功能。
And to keep the price low, the designers removed everything that wasn't really necessary.

37
00:03:46,510 --> 00:03:56,260
但它的设计很聪明，因为许多指令只需几个时钟周期就能完成，所以即使在 1 MHz 左右，
它也能跟运行速度更高的竞争芯片相媲美。
But it was smart about it because many of its instructions finished in just a couple of clock cycles, so even at around 1 MHz,
it could keep up with rival chips running at higher speeds.

38
00:03:56,686 --> 00:04:03,840
顺便说一下，在《辛普森一家》里，Bender 的大脑实际上就是个 6502，
而且它现在还没完全退出历史舞台。
By the way, in Futurama, Bender's Brain is actually a 65.02, and it's still not completely dead either.

39
00:04:04,078 --> 00:04:12,708
一个名为 65C02 的更新版本仍由 Western Design Center 公司生产，用于小型嵌入式设备。
An updated version called the 65C02 is still being made by a company
called Western Design Center, and it's used in small embedded devices.

40
00:04:13,966 --> 00:04:14,692
Z80。
Z80.

41
00:04:15,086 --> 00:04:18,576
Z80 是 6502 最大的对手。
The Z80 was the 6502's biggest rival.

42
00:04:18,766 --> 00:04:28,964
它于 1976 年由 Zilog 公司推出，该公司由 Federico Fajin 创立，
他是 Intel 早期处理器（包括 8080）背后的工程师之一。
It came out in 1976 from a company called Zilog, which was founded by Federico Fajin,
one of the engineers behind Intel's earlier processors, including the 8080.

43
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:33,476
所以他基本上是离开了 Intel，并制造出了自己芯片的改进版。
So he basically left Intel and built a better version of his own chip.

44
00:04:33,870 --> 00:04:41,296
Z80 可以无需任何修改直接运行为 Intel 8080 设计的软件，而且它更便宜，还拥有额外的功能。
The Z80 could run software made for the Intel 8080 without any changes, but it was cheaper and had extra features on top.

45
00:04:41,518 --> 00:04:52,228
这意义重大，因为当时一款流行的商业操作系统 CPM 是为 8080 设计的，
所以所有这些软件都能立即在 Z80 上运行。
And that was a big deal, because a popular business operating system back then called CPM was made for the 8080,
so all of that software instantly worked on the Z80 as well.

46
00:04:52,622 --> 00:05:02,308
正因如此，Z80 最终进入了大量的机器中，比如 ZX Spectrum、
TRS80、Sega Master System，还有最初的 Pac-Man 街机。
Because of this, the Z80 ended up in a huge number of machines, like the ZX Spectrum,
the TRS80, the Sega Master System, and the original Pac-Man arcade machine.

47
00:05:02,702 --> 00:05:09,284
Sega Genesis 也有一颗用于处理声音的 Z80，而任天堂最初的 Game Boy 使用的是它的近亲芯片。
The Sega Genesis also had one inside to handle its sound, and Nintendo's original Game Boy used a close cousin of it.

48
00:05:09,550 --> 00:05:16,292
它甚至出现在 Texas Instruments 的图形计算器中，比如 TI-84，
很多学生至今还在数学课上使用它。
It's even inside Texas Instruments graphing calculators like the TI-84, which a lot of students still use in math class.

49
00:05:16,718 --> 00:05:28,836
与 6502 相比，Z80 拥有更多的指令和更多的内置数据存储槽，这让它更容易编程，
而 6502 则更便宜，且在对应时钟速度下运行极快。
Compared to the 6502, the Z80 had more instructions and more built-in slots for storing data, which made it easier to program,
while the 6502 was cheaper and very quick for its clock speed.

50
00:05:29,198 --> 00:05:32,996
这就是为什么两款芯片的粉丝多年来一直在争论哪一个更好。
That's why fans of both chips argued about which one was better for years.

51
00:05:33,710 --> 00:05:42,816
但在生产 48 年后，Zilog 在 2024 年正式停产独立的 Z80，
最后的一批订单是在那年的 6 月接收的。
But after 48 years of production, Zilog officially discontinued the standalone Z80 in 2024,
with the last orders accepted in June that year.

52
00:05:43,022 --> 00:05:52,292
到了 2026 年，Zilog 的所有者宣布即使是它的新
一代后代 EZ80 也要退役，最后订单将在年底截止。
And in 2026, Zilog's owner announced that even its newer descendant, the EZ80, is being retired too,
with final orders closing at the end of the year.

53
00:05:53,294 --> 00:05:55,056
Motorola 68000。
Motorola 68000.

54
00:05:55,598 --> 00:06:02,468
Motorola 68000 于 1979 年发布，与之前的 8 位芯片相比是一个巨大的飞跃。
The Motorola 68000 was released in 1979, and it was a big jump compared to the 8-bit chips before it.

55
00:06:02,766 --> 00:06:10,276
对于程序员来说，它看起来像是一款 32 位处理器，
因为它的指令和内置存储槽都可以处理 32 位数字。
To programmers, it looked like a 32-bit processor because its instructions and its built-in storage slots worked with 32-bit numbers.

56
00:06:10,670 --> 00:06:20,612
但为了让芯片及其配套的电脑更便宜，它实际上是在用 16 位片段处理大部分工作，
并通过较窄的 16 位路径连接到系统的其余部分。
But to make the chip and the computers built around it cheaper, it did a lot of the actual work in 16-bit pieces and connected to the
rest of the system through a narrower 16-bit path.

57
00:06:20,974 --> 00:06:24,096
你可以把它想象成一台强大的引擎在一条较窄的路上行驶。
Think of it like a powerful engine driving on a narrower road.

58
00:06:24,430 --> 00:06:32,004
这就是为什么 Motorola 称它为 16/32 位处理器，而且恰好它拥有大约 68,000 个晶体管。
That's why Motorola called it a 16 slash 32-bit processor, and fittingly, it had around 68,000 transistors.

59
00:06:32,302 --> 00:06:36,324
程序员非常喜欢它，因为它的指令非常简洁，易于操作。
Programmers loved it because its instructions were clean and easy to work with.

60
00:06:36,846 --> 00:06:44,324
这就是为什么它驱动了新一代拥有图形界面的电脑，在
这些电脑上，你可以用鼠标点击图标，而不是输入命令。
And that's why it powered a new generation of computers with graphical interfaces,
where you click on icons with a mouse instead of typing commands.

61
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:58,372
1984年的初代 Apple Macintosh 使用它，Commodore Amiga 和 Atari ST 也是如此。在游戏领域，
它是 Sega Genesis（也叫 Mega Drive）、Neo Geo 以及大量街机设备中的主要处理器。
The original Apple Macintosh from 1984 used it, and so did the Commodore Amiga and the Atari ST. In gaming,
it was the main processor inside the Sega Genesis, also called the Mega Drive, the Neo Geo, and tons of arcade machines.

62
00:06:58,862 --> 00:07:06,884
它还被广泛用于许多激光打印机甚至一些绘图计算
器，但在 90 年代，更新、更快的架构开始超越它。
It was also used in a lot of laser printers and even some graphing
calculators, but in the 90s, newer and faster designs started to beat it.

63
00:07:07,278 --> 00:07:15,492
Apple 在 1994 年将 Mac 从 68000 系列转向 PowerPC，而其他使用它的家用电脑也逐渐消失了。
Apple moved its Macs from the 68000 family to PowerPC in 1994, and the other home computers that used it slowly disappeared.

64
00:07:15,854 --> 00:07:20,900
尽管如此，基于其设计的芯片在随后的许多年里仍继续用于嵌入式设备。
Still, chips based on its design kept being used in embedded devices for many years after.

65
00:07:21,934 --> 00:07:23,748
IBM System 360。
IBM System 360.

66
00:07:24,078 --> 00:07:34,756
IBM System 360 实际上是这个列表上最古老的一项，它不是单颗芯片，
而是 IBM 在 1964 年宣布的一整套大型机家族。
IBM System 360 is actually the oldest entry on this list, and it's not a single chip,
but a whole family of mainframe computers that IBM announced in 1964.

67
00:07:35,150 --> 00:07:45,476
如果你还不清楚的话，大型机是大型机构用来处理海量数据
的巨大且极其可靠的计算机，比如银行处理数百万笔付款。
And just in case you don't know, a mainframe is a huge, extremely reliable computer that big organizations use to handle massive
amounts of data, like banks processing millions of payments.

68
00:07:45,870 --> 00:07:50,756
在 System 360 出现之前，每款新电脑型号通常都需要专门的软件。
Before the System 360, every new computer model usually needed its own software.

69
00:07:51,150 --> 00:07:56,976
所以如果一家公司升级到更大的电脑，他们就必须扔掉原来的程序，从头开始重新编写。
So if a company upgraded to a bigger computer, they had to throw away their programs and write them again from scratch.

70
00:07:57,262 --> 00:08:01,376
想象一下，每次买新笔记本电脑，你都得重写所有的文档。
Imagine having to rewrite all your documents every time you bought a new laptop.

71
00:08:01,678 --> 00:08:08,388
IBM 通过为整个家族使用统一的架构解决了这个问题，从小型廉价型号到大型高性能型号。
IBM fixed this by using one architecture for the entire family, from small, cheap models to huge, powerful ones.

72
00:08:08,782 --> 00:08:12,900
因此，为其中一个 System 360 编写的程序可以在任何型号上运行。
So a program written for one system 360 could run on any of them.

73
00:08:13,136 --> 00:08:14,884
但这是一场巨大的豪赌。
But this was a massive gamble.

74
00:08:15,214 --> 00:08:23,876
IBM 花费了大约 50 亿美元来开发它，这甚至超过了公
司一整年的收入，所以如果失败了，IBM 可能会倒闭。
IBM spent around $5 billion developing it, which was more than the company
was making in an entire year, so if it failed, IBM could have gone under.

75
00:08:24,174 --> 00:08:25,956
幸运的是，它获得了巨大的回报。
Luckily, it paid off big time.

76
00:08:26,414 --> 00:08:32,096
它还让 8 位字节成为了标准，直到今天，它仍是计算机衡量数据的基本单位。
It also made the 8-bit byte the standard, which is still the basic unit computers use to measure data today.

77
00:08:32,332 --> 00:08:37,828
NASA 甚至还使用 System 360 计算机在阿波罗登月任务期间支持任务控制。
And NASA even used System 360 computers to support mission control during the Apollo Moon missions.

78
00:08:38,254 --> 00:08:41,696
最酷的部分是，IBM 从未破坏过这种兼容性。
The coolest part is, IBM never broke that compatibility.

79
00:08:42,062 --> 00:08:54,084
今天的 IBM Z 大型机，比如 2025 年发布的 Z17，都是 System 360 的直接后代，在许多情况下，
几十年前为它编写的程序现在仍能在上面运行。
Today's IBM Z mainframes, like the Z17 released in 2025, are direct descendants of the System360, and in many cases,
programs written for it decades ago can still run on them.

80
00:08:54,510 --> 00:09:00,452
根据 IBM 的说法，全球约 70% 按价值计算的金融交易都是通过这些机器完成的。
According to IBM, around 70% of the world's financial transactions by value go through these machines.

81
00:09:00,910 --> 00:09:09,124
所以每当你用卡付款或从 ATM 机取钱时，很有可能正是 System 360 的曾曾孙辈在处理这些操作。
So whenever you pay with a card or take money out of an ATM, there's a
good chance a great great grandchild of the System360 is handling it.

82
00:09:10,126 --> 00:09:11,044
8051。
8051.

83
00:09:11,534 --> 00:09:15,812
Intel 8051 可能是你从未听说过但使用频率最高的芯片。
The Intel 8051 is probably the most used chip you've never heard of.

84
00:09:16,110 --> 00:09:21,636
它由 Intel 在 1980 年发布，它不是普通的处理器，而是一个微控制器。
It was released by Intel in 1980, and it's not a regular processor, but a microcontroller.

85
00:09:21,902 --> 00:09:28,324
区别在于，普通的处理器只是大脑，它需要独立的内存和其他芯片配合才能工作。
The difference is, a normal processor is just the brain, and it needs separate memory and other chips around it to work.

86
00:09:28,654 --> 00:09:36,900
但微控制器将大脑、少量内存、定时器以及按钮和传感器的连接全部集成在单颗芯片上。
But a microcontroller puts the brain, a small amount of memory, timers,
and connections for things like buttons and sensors all on one single chip.

87
00:09:37,358 --> 00:09:44,464
所以它基本上就是一个为了控制特定任务而制造的微型计算机，而这正是 8051 的擅长领域。
So it's basically a whole tiny computer made to control one specific job, and that's exactly what the 8051 is good at.

88
00:09:44,686 --> 00:09:51,744
它不需要很强大，只需要便宜、可靠且简单，比如读取你按下了哪个键或控制电机。
It doesn't need to be powerful, it just needs to be cheap, reliable,
and simple, like reading which key you pressed or controlling a motor.

89
00:09:52,014 --> 00:09:58,532
这就是为什么它被用于电脑鼠标、键盘、家用电器、汽车，甚至在蓝牙芯片内部。
That's why it's been used in things like computer mice, keyboards, home appliances, cars, and even inside Bluetooth chips.

90
00:09:58,990 --> 00:10:04,676
Intel 自己在 2007 年停止生产 8051，但这完全没能终结它。
Intel itself stopped making the 8051 in 2007, but that didn't kill it at all.

91
00:10:04,974 --> 00:10:13,904
还有 20 多家公司生产能理解完全相同指令的芯片，而且
它的设计甚至被集成到更大的芯片中作为小型辅助核心。
More than 20 other companies make chips that understand the exact same instructions,
and its design is even built into bigger chips as a small helper core.

92
00:10:14,094 --> 00:10:19,556
它在很多工程学院里仍被教授，因为它简单且文档极其完善。
It's also still taught in a lot of engineering schools because it's simple and extremely well documented.

93
00:10:19,886 --> 00:10:26,660
所以尽管它是 1980 年的 8 位设计，但你现在使用的某些设备里很有可能就藏着一颗 8051。
So even though it's an 8-bit design from 1980, there's a good chance something you use today has an 8051 inside.

94
00:10:27,726 --> 00:10:28,100
MIPS。
MIPS.

95
00:10:28,686 --> 00:10:34,820
MIPS 始于 1981 年，是斯坦福大学的一个研究项目，由亨尼西领导。
MIPS started in 1981 as a research project at Stanford University, led by John Hennessy.

96
00:10:34,958 --> 00:10:39,904
这就是我们需要聊聊 RISC 的地方，它的全称是精简指令集计算机。
And this is where we need to talk about RISC, which stands for Reduced Instruction Set Computer.

97
00:10:40,110 --> 00:10:46,116
记得 x86 是 CISC，拥有大量复杂的指令，而 RISC 则走向了相反的方向。
Remember how X86 is Cisq, with lots of complex instructions, RISC goes the opposite way.

98
00:10:46,446 --> 00:10:50,864
它使用一小组简单的指令，每条指令都能非常快速地完成。
It uses a smaller set of simple instructions that can each be done very quickly.

99
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:53,092
一个很好的思考方式是做菜。
A good way to think about it is cooking.

100
00:10:53,358 --> 00:11:00,932
CISC 芯片就像一个懂「给我做个三明治」这种订单的厨师，但这个订单背后涉及很多复杂的工序。
A Cisq chip is like a chef who understands an order like Make Me a
Sandwich, but that one order involves a lot of work behind the scenes.

101
00:11:01,326 --> 00:11:06,532
RISC 芯片只理解简单的步骤，比如拿面包、加奶酪、封口。
A RISC chip only understands simple steps like grab the bread, add the cheese, close it.

102
00:11:06,784 --> 00:11:12,464
但它每一步都做得非常快且流畅，所以整个三明治最终还是很快就做好了。
But it does each step so fast and so smoothly that the whole sandwich ends up done quickly anyway.

103
00:11:12,718 --> 00:11:17,984
而且因为芯片本身更简单，所以更容易设计，而且通常更省电。
And since the chip itself is simpler, it's also easier to design and usually uses less power.

104
00:11:18,382 --> 00:11:25,744
亨尼西和他的团队把这个项目变成了一家公司，他们的第一款芯片 R2000 于 1985 年发布。
Hennessy and his team turned the project into a company, and their first chip, the R2000, was announced in 1985.

105
00:11:26,030 --> 00:11:28,064
在 90 年代，MIPS 变得非常庞大。
In the 90s, MIPS became huge.

106
00:11:28,526 --> 00:11:37,476
生产高性能工作站的 Silicon Graphics 公司在它的机器中使用了 MIPS，
而那些正是当时好莱坞工作室用来做特效的电脑。
Silicon Graphics, a company making powerful workstations, used MIPS in its machines,
and those were the computers Hollywood Studios used for special effects back then.

107
00:11:37,806 --> 00:11:45,284
在游戏领域，最初的 PlayStation、Nintendo 64、
PlayStation 2 和 PSP 都运行在 MIPS 处理器上。
In gaming, the original PlayStation, the Nintendo 64, the PlayStation 2, and the PSP all ran on MIPS processors.

108
00:11:45,806 --> 00:11:51,044
它还在互联网路由器、电视盒子和其他家用电子产品中使用了很多年。
It was also used for years in internet routers, TV boxes, and other home electronics.

109
00:11:51,406 --> 00:11:58,852
有趣的事实是，亨尼西后来成为了斯坦福大学的校长，并获得了图灵奖，
这基本上就是计算机科学界的诺贝尔奖。
Fun fact, John Hennessy later became the president of Stanford and won the Turing Award,
which is basically the Nobel Prize of Computer Science.

110
00:11:59,374 --> 00:12:04,452
然而，MIPS 慢慢被 ARM 赶超，尤其是智能手机普及之后。
However, MIPS slowly lost ground to ARM, especially once smartphones took over.

111
00:12:04,718 --> 00:12:12,228
这家公司经历了多次所有权变更，并在 2021 年停止开发新的 MIPS 设计，转而采用 RISC-V。
The company went through several owners, and in 2021 it stopped developing new MIPS designs and switched to RISC-V instead.

112
00:12:12,590 --> 00:12:16,740
然后在 2025 年，芯片制造商 Global Foundries 收购了它。
Then in 2025, the chip manufacturer Global Foundries bought it.

113
00:12:17,262 --> 00:12:22,244
所以公司名字还在，但 MIPS 架构本身基本上已经退役了。
So the company name still exists, but the MIPS architecture itself has basically been retired.

114
00:12:23,278 --> 00:12:24,224
PowerPC。
PowerPC.

115
00:12:24,590 --> 00:12:30,308
PowerPC 是在 1991 年由 Apple、IBM 和 Motorola 组成的联盟创建的。
PowerPC was created in 1991 by an alliance between Apple, IBM, and Motorola.

116
00:12:30,544 --> 00:12:39,204
它是基于 IBM 用于其服务器的自有 Power 处理器，目标是构建一款快速的 RISC 芯片，
在个人电脑领域与 Intel 竞争。
It was based on IBM's own power processors used in its servers, and the goal was
to build a fast RISC chip that could compete with Intel in personal computers.

117
00:12:39,630 --> 00:12:49,316
Apple 在 1994 年将 Mac 切换到 PowerPC，此后十多年里，Mac 都运行在它上面，
包括 1998 年那款色彩缤纷的 iMac G3。
Apple switched its Macs to PowerPC in 1994, and for over a decade, Macs ran on it, including the colorful iMac G3 from 1998.

118
00:12:49,646 --> 00:12:51,876
但最终，Apple 遇到了问题。
But eventually, Apple ran into a problem.

119
00:12:52,366 --> 00:12:59,780
更新的 PowerPC 芯片发热过高且功耗太大，难以塞进超薄笔记本，而 Intel 的芯片一直在进步。
The newer PowerPC chips were running too hot and using too much power
to fit into thin laptops, while Intel's chips kept getting better.

120
00:13:00,046 --> 00:13:06,244
因此在 2005 年，Apple 宣布转向 Intel，到 2006 年就完成了切换。
So in 2005, Apple announced it was moving to Intel, and the Switch was done by 2006.

121
00:13:06,574 --> 00:13:11,492
但 PowerPC 并没有在那之后就真的消失，因为它接管了游戏主机。
But PowerPC didn't really die after that because it took over game consoles instead.

122
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:16,324
任天堂的 GameCube、Wii 和 Wii U 都使用了 PowerPC 芯片。
The Nintendo GameCube, the Wii, and the Wii U all used PowerPC chips.

123
00:13:16,878 --> 00:13:25,860
Xbox 360 搭载了由 IBM 制造的 3 核 PowerPC 处理器，而
PlayStation 3 的 Cell 处理器是围绕 PowerPC Core 2 构建的。
The Xbox 360 had a 3-core PowerPC processor made by IBM, and the PlayStation 3's cell processor was built around a PowerPC Core 2.

124
00:13:26,158 --> 00:13:32,324
所以有一段时间，三大主流主机同时都在运行 PowerPC，甚至它还去了火星。
So for a while, all three major consoles were running on PowerPC at the same time, and it even went to Mars.

125
00:13:32,814 --> 00:13:42,724
NASA 的好奇号和毅力号火星车都使用名为 RAD 750 的计算机，
它正是基于那台 1998 年 iMac 所使用的 PowerPC 750 芯片。
NASA's Curiosity and Perseverance rovers both use a computer called the
RAD 750, which is based on the same PowerPC 750 chip from that 1998 iMac.

126
00:13:43,214 --> 00:13:52,624
按今天的标准来看它很慢，最高运行速度只有 200 MHz，但它是专门为在太空环境中抵御辐射而
设计的，每台造价超过 20 万美元。
It's slow by today's standards, running at up to 200 MHz, but it's specially
built to survive the radiation in space, and each one costs over $200,000.

127
00:13:53,358 --> 00:14:02,948
如今，PowerPC 基本从消费类产品中消失了，但 IBM 仍在其高端服务器中使用其架构，
也就是「大兄弟」PowerPC 的来源。
Today, PowerPC is mostly gone from consumer products, but IBM still uses its power architecture,
the Big Brother PowerPC came from in its high end servers.

128
00:14:04,142 --> 00:14:04,964
DEC Alpha。
DEC Alpha.

129
00:14:05,422 --> 00:14:13,796
Deck Alpha 是由 Digital Equipment Corporation（简称 DEC）制造的 64 位 RISC 架构，
DEC 是当时最大的计算机公司之一。
Deck Alpha was a 64-bit RISC architecture made by Digital Equipment Corporation, or DEC,
which was one of the biggest computer companies of its time.

130
00:14:14,062 --> 00:14:21,476
它在 1992 年发布，目标很简单：成为世界上最快的处理器，而且有一段时间它确实做到了。
It launched in 1992, and the goal was simple: be the fastest processor in the world, and for a while it actually was.

131
00:14:22,030 --> 00:14:29,764
Alpha 芯片在纯粹的速度上远超竞争对手，它们被用于强大的服务器、科学研究和高端工作站。
Alpha chips were way ahead of their competitors in raw speed, and they were
used in powerful servers, scientific research, and high-end workstations.

132
00:14:30,126 --> 00:14:35,120
它甚至能运行 Windows NT，而在那时，只有极少数非 Intel 芯片能做到这一点。
It could even run Windows NT, which only a handful of non-Intel chips could do back then.

133
00:14:35,406 --> 00:14:41,028
Alpha 服务器还驱动了 Alta Vista，这是在 Google 接管之前最流行的搜索引擎之一。
Alpha servers also powered Alta Vista, one of the most popular search engines before Google took over.

134
00:14:41,230 --> 00:14:43,108
但仅仅最快是不够的。
But being the fastest wasn't enough.

135
00:14:43,534 --> 00:14:51,588
Alpha 机器非常昂贵，而且很少有软件是为它们开发的，微
软甚至在 Windows 2000 发布前就停止了对 Alpha 的支持。
Alpha machines were expensive, there wasn't much software made for them,
and Microsoft dropped Alpha support before Windows 2000 even came out.

136
00:14:51,886 --> 00:14:55,012
再加上 DEC 本身在财务上也陷入了困境。
On top of that, DEC itself was struggling financially.

137
00:14:55,342 --> 00:15:00,260
1998 年，它被 Compaq 收购，但 Compaq 并不真的知道该拿 Alpha 怎么办。
In 1998, it was bought by Compaq, which didn't really know what to do with Alpha.

138
00:15:00,558 --> 00:15:10,020
随后在 2001 年，Compaq 宣布将停止开发 Alpha，转而采用 Intel 的 Itanium，
正如你稍后会看到的，这并不是个明智的选择。
Then in 2001, Compaq announced it would stop developing Alpha and move to
Intel's Itanium instead, which, as you'll see in a moment, wasn't the best bet.

139
00:15:10,446 --> 00:15:13,156
尽管如此，Alpha 并没有无影无踪地消失。
Still, Alpha didn't just vanish without a trace.

140
00:15:13,710 --> 00:15:19,748
它的许多理念和工程师最终流向了其他公司，包括 AMD 和 Intel。
Many of its ideas and engineers ended up at other companies, including both AMD and Intel.

141
00:15:20,078 --> 00:15:31,972
一些参与 Alpha 开发的工程师后来帮助构建了 AMD 的 Athlon 处理器，
甚至重用了 Alpha 的连接设计，Athlon 帮助 AMD 最终成为了 Intel 的强劲对手。
Some of the engineers who worked on Alpha went on to help build AMD's Athlon processors,
which even reused a connection design from Alpha, and the Athlon helped AMD finally become a serious rival to Intel.

142
00:15:32,942 --> 00:15:33,700
Itanium。
Itanium.

143
00:15:34,318 --> 00:15:37,892
Itanium 是 Intel 用来取代 x86 的重大尝试。
Itanium was Intel's big attempt to replace X86.

144
00:15:38,286 --> 00:15:48,516
它是与 HP 共同开发的，计划是创建一个全新的 64 位
架构，称为 IA64，先接管服务器，最终接管所有领域。
It was developed together with HP, and the plan was to create a brand new 64-bit
architecture called IA64 that would take over servers first and eventually everything else.

145
00:15:49,070 --> 00:15:53,700
第一款 Itanium 芯片在 2001 年发布，比计划晚了两年。
The first Itanium chip came out in 2001, two years later than planned.

146
00:15:54,062 --> 00:15:56,320
其背后的理念很巧妙，但风险很大。
The idea behind it was clever but risky.

147
00:15:56,560 --> 00:16:03,280
通常情况下，现代 CPU 会在运行时自行判断哪些指令可以同时执行以提高速度。
Normally, a modern CPU figures out on its own, while it's running, which instructions it can do at the same time to go faster.

148
00:16:03,598 --> 00:16:10,084
Itanium 把这项工作移交给了编译器，也就是在程序运行前将其转换为指令的软件。
Itanium moved that job to the compiler, which is the software that translates a program into instructions before it even runs.

149
00:16:10,638 --> 00:16:14,788
你可以把它想象成在出门前，就把整趟公路旅行的每分钟计划都安排好。
Think of it like planning an entire road trip minute by minute before you leave home.

150
00:16:15,118 --> 00:16:17,028
如果没有交通堵塞，那它就是完美的。
If there's no traffic, it's perfect.

151
00:16:17,390 --> 00:16:22,788
但真实的道路是不可预测的，同样，真实的程序也是不可预测的。
But real roads are unpredictable, and in the same way, real programs are unpredictable too.

152
00:16:23,022 --> 00:16:28,196
编译器在提前规划方面的能力始终没能达到足够高的水平，所以性能往往没能达到宣传的效果。
Compilers never got good enough at planning ahead, so the performance often didn't live up to the hype.

153
00:16:28,654 --> 00:16:35,620
除此之外，Itanium 运行旧的 x86 程序速度很慢，而这正是大多数企业实际使用的程序。
On top of that, Itanium was slow at running old X86 programs, which is what most businesses actually used.

154
00:16:36,014 --> 00:16:44,932
接着在 2003 年，AMD 发布了 x86 的 64 位版本，它能全速运行所有旧软件，而且成本低得多。
Then in 2003, AMD released its 64-bit version of X86, which ran all the old software at full speed and cost way less.

155
00:16:45,294 --> 00:16:52,324
所以大多数客户索性选择了那个，甚至连 Intel 最
后也采用了 AMD 的方案来制作自己的 Xeon 处理器。
So most customers simply picked that instead, and even Intel ended up using AMD's approach for its own Xeon processors.

156
00:16:52,782 --> 00:16:58,852
这就是为什么人们开玩笑叫它「Itanic」，就像泰坦尼克号一样，
一艘巨大且昂贵但最终沉没的船。
That's why people jokingly called it the Itanic, like the Titanic, a huge, expensive ship that sank.

157
00:16:59,246 --> 00:17:06,404
Intel 在 2021 年出货了最后一批 Itanium 芯片，而在 2024 年，Linux 正式移除了对它的支持。
Intel shipped the last Itanium chips in 2021, and in 2024, Linux officially removed support for it.

158
00:17:07,470 --> 00:17:07,839
ARM。
ARM.

159
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:12,164
ARM 是地球上基本上每部智能手机内部的架构。
ARM is the architecture inside basically every smartphone on the planet.

160
00:17:12,430 --> 00:17:21,028
它始于 1985 年的 Acorn Computers，这是一家生产 BBC
Micro 的英国公司，顺便提一下，那是运行在 6502 上的。
It started in 1985 at Acorn Computers, a British company that made the BBC Micro, which, by the way, ran on the 6502.

161
00:17:21,390 --> 00:17:31,840
Acorn 想要为它的下一台电脑设计更快的芯片，于是两名工程师 Sophie Wilson 和 Steve
Ferber 设计了自己的 RISC 处理器，并称之为 Acorn RISC Machine，简称 ARM。
Acorn wanted a faster chip for its next computer, so two engineers, Sophie Wilson and Steve Ferber,
designed their own RISC processor and called it the Acorn RISC Machine, or ARM.

162
00:17:32,174 --> 00:17:36,004
最有趣的部分是，ARM 最大的优势是偶然发现的。
And the funniest part is, ARM's biggest strength was discovered by accident.

163
00:17:36,494 --> 00:17:41,440
当 Steve Ferber 测试第一颗芯片时，他的仪表显示它根本不耗电。
When Steve Ferber tested the very first chip, his meter showed it was using no power at all.

164
00:17:41,774 --> 00:17:50,532
结果发现测试板有故障，甚至没有给处理器供电，但芯片依然在运行，
因为它利用了从周围电路中渗入的一点点微弱电流。
It turned out the test board was faulty and wasn't even sending power to the processor,
but the chip was still running on the tiny bit of electricity leaking in from the circuits around it.

165
00:17:50,830 --> 00:17:52,132
这就是它的能效。
That's how efficient it was.

166
00:17:52,750 --> 00:18:00,612
那时，低功耗甚至不是目标，但正是这一点让 ARM 在后来非常适合手机和其他电池供电的设备。
Back then, low power wasn't even the goal, but that's exactly what
made ARM perfect for phones and other battery-powered devices later on.

167
00:18:00,974 --> 00:18:07,104
让 ARM 与众不同的还有一点，就是在其几乎整个历史中，这家公司根本不卖芯片。
Another thing that makes ARM different is that for almost its entire history, the company didn't sell chips at all.

168
00:18:07,344 --> 00:18:18,144
相反，它负责设计并出售授权，这样像 Apple、Qualcomm、
Samsung 和 MediaTek 等公司就可以制造自己的 ARM 芯片，并为每颗售出的芯片支付少量的费用。
Instead, it designs them and sells licenses, so other companies like Apple, Qualcomm, Samsung,
and MediaTek can build their own ARM chips and pay a small fee for every chip they sell.

169
00:18:18,414 --> 00:18:21,764
这有点像卖食谱而不是开餐厅。
It's kind of like selling a recipe instead of opening a restaurant.

170
00:18:22,190 --> 00:18:27,984
这种模式非常成功，因为到目前为止已经出货了超过 3000 亿颗基于 ARM 的芯片。
And this worked incredibly well because more than 300 billion ARM-based chips have been shipped so far.

171
00:18:28,238 --> 00:18:34,468
直到 2026 年，ARM 才终于开始销售自己的芯片，一款用于 AI 数据中心的处理器。
Only in 2026 did ARM finally start selling a chip of its own, a processor for AI data centers.

172
00:18:34,862 --> 00:18:36,804
如今，ARM 不仅仅存在于手机中。
Today, ARM isn't just in phones.

173
00:18:37,358 --> 00:18:45,956
Apple 在 2020 年将其 Mac 从 Intel 切换到了自己的 ARM 系列 M 系列芯片，
它们以快速且电池续航极长而闻名。
Apple switched its Macs from Intel to its own ARM-based M series chips in
2020, and they're known for being fast while having really long battery life.

174
00:18:46,478 --> 00:18:56,420
Nintendo Switch、Raspberry Pi、平板电脑、智能手表、智能电视、汽车，
甚至像 Amazon 这样的公司的巨型云服务器也运行在 ARM 上。
The Nintendo Switch, the Raspberry Pi, tablets, smartwatches, smart TVs,
cars, and even huge cloud servers from companies like Amazon run on ARM too.

175
00:18:56,718 --> 00:18:59,652
现在还有搭载 ARM 芯片的 Windows 笔记本电脑。
There are also Windows laptops with ARM chips now.

176
00:19:00,014 --> 00:19:07,984
主要的缺点是，很多旧的 Windows 应用和游戏是为 x86 设计的，
所以在 ARM 上它们必须在运行时进行转换。
The main downside is that a lot of older Windows apps and games were made for x86, so on ARM they have to be translated on the fly.

177
00:19:08,334 --> 00:19:13,508
其中一些运行变慢，有些甚至完全无法运行，尤其是带有反作弊软件的游戏。
Some of them run slower, and some don't work at all, especially games with anti-cheat software.

178
00:19:14,510 --> 00:19:15,104
RISC V。
RISC V.

179
00:19:15,790 --> 00:19:21,412
RISC V，读作 RISC V，始于 2010 年的加州大学伯克利分校。
RISC V, pronounced RISC V, started in 2010 at the University of California Berkeley.

180
00:19:21,678 --> 00:19:26,692
名字里的 5 是因为它是伯克利产出的第五代 RISC 设计。
The 5 in the name is there because it was the fifth generation of RISC designs to come out of Berkeley.

181
00:19:26,958 --> 00:19:33,220
其中参与人员之一是戴维·帕特森，也就是和来自MIPS的亨尼西共同获得图灵奖的那个人。
And one of the people involved was David Patterson, the same guy who shared that Turing Award with John Hennessy from MIPS.

182
00:19:33,742 --> 00:19:37,344
RISC-V 的特别之处在于它是完全开放且免费的。
What makes RISC-V special is that it's completely open and free.

183
00:19:37,582 --> 00:19:41,252
在x86架构下，只有少数几家公司被允许制造芯片。
With X86, only a few companies are allowed to make the chips.

184
00:19:41,710 --> 00:19:44,548
而在ARM架构下，你必须支付授权费和专利费。
With ARM, you have to pay license fees and royalties.

185
00:19:44,846 --> 00:19:50,064
但有了RISC-V，任何人都可以设计芯片而无需申请许可或向任何人付费。
But with RISC V, anyone can design a chip with it without asking permission or paying anyone.

186
00:19:50,350 --> 00:19:54,372
就像Linux是一个任何人都可以使用和修改的免费操作系统一样。
Just like Linux is a free operating system that anyone can use and modify.

187
00:19:54,670 --> 00:19:58,052
RISC-V 是一个任何人都可以在其基础上进行开发的免费指令集。
RISC V is a free instruction set that anyone can build on.

188
00:19:58,382 --> 00:20:05,540
它由总部位于瑞士的非营利组织 RISC-V International 管理，因此没有任何一家公司能控制它。
It's managed by a nonprofit organization called RISC V International, based in Switzerland, so no single company controls it.

189
00:20:05,838 --> 00:20:11,300
这就是为什么很多公司都在转向它，既是为了省钱，也是为了避免依赖于他人。
That's why a lot of companies are jumping on it, both to save money and to avoid depending on someone else.

190
00:20:11,664 --> 00:20:22,436
例如，NVIDIA 在其显卡内部使用小型 RISC-V 核心来处理
后台的管理任务，到2024年，它已经出货了超过十亿个。
For example, NVIDIA uses small RISC-V cores inside its graphics cards to handle management tasks behind the scenes, and by 2024,
it had already shipped over a billion of them.

191
00:20:22,958 --> 00:20:31,204
Western Digital 在存储设备中使用它，它也出现在智
能家居设备的廉价芯片中，比如一些较新的ESP32型号。
Western Digital uses it in storage devices, and it's showing up in
cheap chips for smart home gadgets, like some of the newer ESP32 models.

192
00:20:31,438 --> 00:20:32,452
还记得MIPS吗？
And remember MIPS?

193
00:20:32,864 --> 00:20:34,784
甚至那家公司也转向了RISC-V。
Even that company switched to RISC-V.

194
00:20:35,246 --> 00:20:37,476
不过，RISC-V 仍然很年轻。
However, RISC V is still young.

195
00:20:37,934 --> 00:20:44,516
既然任何人都可以基于它进行开发，公司经常会添加自己的自定义功能，而且软件支持仍在赶超。
Since anyone can build on it, companies often add their own custom extras, and software support is still catching up.

196
00:20:44,782 --> 00:20:48,420
这就是为什么你目前还不太能在主流手机或笔记本电脑上找到它。
That's why you won't really find it in mainstream phones or laptops yet.

197
00:20:48,686 --> 00:20:59,716
目前，它大多隐藏在其他设备中执行较小的任务，但它的增长非常迅速，
许多人相信它未来可能成为ARM和x86的强劲对手。
For now, it's mostly hidden inside other devices doing smaller jobs, but it's growing really fast,
and a lot of people believe it could become a serious rival to ARM and x86 in the future.

